  "title": "Puja",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "About 8% of Bangladeshis are Hindu, and **দুর্গাপূজা** (*durgapuja*) is their biggest **উৎসব** (festival). Thousands of **পূজা মণ্ডপ** (temporary pavilions) are set up across the country, each with a clay **প্রতিমা** of the goddess Durga. Visitors of all faiths go to see them.\n\nOn the last day the images are immersed in the river; afterwards friends greet each other with **শুভ বিজয়া** and sweets. With Hindu friends, **নমস্কার** is the natural hello.\n\nIn Bangladesh the official slogan is **ধর্ম যার যার, উৎসব সবার** — 'religion is each person's own, festivals belong to everyone'.\n\n**Kolkata:** spoken **পুজো** (*pujo*); Durga Puja is *the* festival of the year.",
